Found while working on https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/pull/106 (first seen in link-foundation/link-cli#98), with `platform-mem` 0.3.0 (`main` is the same commit, c373135) and `doublets` 0.5.0.

## Repro

A `doublets` store on `FileMapped` loses every link when it is reopened:

```rust
use doublets::{mem::FileMapped, unit::{LinkPart, Store}, Doublets};

let path = "/tmp/exp.doublets";
let _ = std::fs::remove_file(path);
{
    let mut store = Store::<u32, _>::new(FileMapped::<LinkPart<u32>>::from_path(path)?)?;
    let a = store.create_link(0, 0)?;
    store.create_link(a, a)?;
    println!("wrote count={}", store.count());           // 2
}
println!("file size = {}", std::fs::metadata(path)?.len()); // 33554432
{
    let store = Store::<u32, _>::new(FileMapped::<LinkPart<u32>>::from_path(path)?)?;
    println!("reopened count={}", store.count());        // 0, expected 2
    println!("link 1 = {:?}", store.get_link(1));        // None
}
```

## Root cause

[`FileMapped::grow`](https://github.com/linksplatform/mem-rs/blob/c373135da4dec66c946b504bb455af4aec732816/src/file_mapped.rs#L74-L107) computes `inited`, the number of new elements that are already backed by bytes in the file, and passes it to the fill closure. The default [`RawMem::grow_filled`](https://github.com/linksplatform/mem-rs/blob/c373135da4dec66c946b504bb455af4aec732816/src/raw_mem.rs#L242-L252) ignores it and fills the whole region:

```rust
self.grow(cap, |_, (_, uninit)| {
    uninit::fill(uninit, value);
})
```

[`grow_zeroed`](https://github.com/linksplatform/mem-rs/blob/c373135da4dec66c946b504bb455af4aec732816/src/raw_mem.rs#L197-L203) does the same with zeros. `doublets` resizes through `grow_filled` ([`resize_mem`](https://github.com/linksplatform/doublets-rs/blob/1d54fd692960258b9b72380e67e2c4f6369372bf/doublets/src/mem/mod.rs#L26-L42)), so the header and every link read back from the file are overwritten with `Default::default()`.

[`grow_filled_exact`](https://github.com/linksplatform/mem-rs/blob/c373135da4dec66c946b504bb455af4aec732816/src/raw_mem.rs#L254-L269) fills only `uninit[inited..]` and keeps the data. link-cli works around the bug with a wrapper that forwards `grow_filled` to `grow_filled_exact`: [`PersistentFileMapped`](https://github.com/link-foundation/link-cli/blob/main/rust/src/storage/file_mem.rs).

## Suggested fix

Either:

- make the default `grow_filled` and `grow_zeroed` skip `inited`, so the safe methods never destroy persisted data; or
- have `doublets` call `grow_filled_exact` (it is `unsafe`, but `FileMapped` computes `inited` itself).

The first fixes every consumer. Either way, a test that writes, drops and reopens a `FileMapped` would keep it fixed.

If type has value there is Value link which points from type to `String|Number|Object`. We should do the same for `File`

Right now there is no `Value` link that points from `AsyncFile` type
```js
await deep.select({
    from_id: await deep.id("@deep-foundation/core", "AsyncFile"),
    type_id: await deep.id("@deep-foundation/core", "Value")
})
{data: Array(0), loading: false, networkStatus: 7}
```
